# DIBAY Supabase SSOT

Canonical docs: `docs/dibay-supabase-final-production-hard-lock.md` · `docs/dibay-supabase-fd6-storage-hard-lock.md` · `docs/dibay-existing-live-schema-authority-convention.md`.

Historical SHA / dpl / P0-P1 forensic counts are **not** execution authority (TIER 4).

## Storage / media

- Persistable media refs only — `blob:` / `localhost` / `undefined` never become DB authority
- Invalid refs must not be prefixed onto `/storage/v1/object/public/`
- Do not invent AVIF `.feed.webp` derivatives
- No bulk orphan delete · bucket reset · mass path rewrite · mass NULL of media refs
- No image URL fallback that hides broken data
- RLS/policy change only on new Storage security contradiction

## Product / schema security (preserve)

- Do not reopen full Supabase forensic because historical dashboard counts are non-zero
- Speculative repair · RLS weakening · timeout/rate-limit raise to hide defects — forbidden
- Do not convert NOT_PROVEN or FIXTURE_BLOCKED into PASS
- Existing-live tables: MATCH → NO-OP; DRIFT/EXTRA → FAIL-FAST (no silent ALTER); MISSING → BLOCK (no auto-CREATE on recovery)
- Authority fingerprints: `supabase/schema-authority/` · `npm run verify:schema-authority`

## Reopen

Only on a new current Production P0/P1 · reproduced regression · schema/security/migration authority change · Owner reopen.
